{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas","id":865860,"title":"Beast Dark Eras Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-15T02:48:54-07:00","id":865860,"title":"Beast Dark Eras Ideas","content":"I'm fiddling with an era hopping game inspired by &quot;Dark Eras&quot;. Besides the Reconstruction Era we're getting in the Dark Eras Companion, what are your choices for compelling fits for BtP. My best developed ideas so far:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">1) Ivan the Terrible's Russia. The uniting of diverse peoples as kin under the force of a powerful feared Apex. Kind of on the nose really</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2) Vampire crossover for the Jazz Age; Lovecraftian racism at the height of post-civil war racial violence in the US set against the intrigue and beauty of the Harlem Renaissance.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T03:39:43-07:00","id":865873,"title":"","content":"Have you read Ride to Damascus (As always, link in my index)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T05:00:59-07:00","id":865887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas#post865860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fiddling with an era hopping game inspired by &quot;Dark Eras&quot;. Besides the Reconstruction Era we're getting in the Dark Eras Companion, what are your choices for compelling fits for BtP. My best developed ideas so far:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">1) Ivan the Terrible's Russia. The uniting of diverse peoples as kin under the force of a powerful feared Apex. Kind of on the nose really</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2) Vampire crossover for the Jazz Age; Lovecraftian racism at the height of post-civil war racial violence in the US set against the intrigue and beauty of the Harlem Renaissance.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Both good ideas!<br /> <br /> A number of periods from the DE books can easily feature Beast as well (the Alexandrian, Stone Age ones come to mind).<br /> <br /> Since Beast is all about fear and family, what about the second red scare and McCarthyism?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T05:04:58-07:00","id":865889,"title":"","content":"double post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","user":"Daigotsu Max","date":". 04-15-2016, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T05:07:18-07:00","id":865893,"title":"","content":"To the Strongest definitely. Sundered World I'm still wrestling with a bit because I feel like the Begotten get overshadowed by the Pangeans hunting through Astral and physical world alike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T00:35:22-07:00","id":866294,"title":"","content":"I think the Hittite Empire during the Bronze Age Collapse would be a good choice because it was a time when the civilizations along the Mediterranean all failed at once. The Bronze Age collapse was probably one of the last times Beasts were actually relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T00:44:36-07:00","id":866297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas?p=866294#post866294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Hittite Empire during the Bronze Age Collapse would be a good choice because it was a time when the civilizations along the Mediterranean all failed at once. The Bronze Age collapse was probably one of the last times Beasts were actually relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would presumably be fitting as a time where their conflicts with Heroes got particularly recorded after being passed down to later Greeks.<br /> <br /> Could tie it together with Changeling and make it a big deal that the first forging of iron happens and the breaking of the Contract of Iron makes a big shift for Arcadia, and you see the birth of what will be-called Courts in this era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T00:52:11-07:00","id":866302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas?p=866294#post866294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Hittite Empire during the Bronze Age Collapse would be a good choice because it was a time when the civilizations along the Mediterranean all failed at once. The Bronze Age collapse was probably one of the last times Beasts were actually relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be absolutely willing to look past my dislike of Beast if it got a Bronze Age Collapse setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T21:44:22-07:00","id":866661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas?p=866294#post866294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Hittite Empire during the Bronze Age Collapse would be a good choice because it was a time when the civilizations along the Mediterranean all failed at once. The Bronze Age collapse was probably one of the last times Beasts were actually relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll third this one, especially with the Ling add-in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the Storyteller!&quot; <hr /><a href=\"https://www.fromdusktilljawn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">From Dusk 'til Jawn</a> - 2e nWoD game set in Philadelphia<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gravenlore.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Graven Lore</a> - 2e multi-venue nWoD game<br /> <a href=\"http://newhaven.mindrealms.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Haven</a> - 2e nWoD game set in southern Maine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/951-caelene","name":"Caelene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T00:27:14-07:00","id":866708,"title":"","content":"Here's another idea: the Mongol Empire era. I mean for many of its subjects, the Mongols must have been this alien, all powerful enemy which came and took what it wanted, reshaping society as it went... sounds pretty Beast-y to me!<br /> <br /> @Glamourweaver: I'm beginning to wonder if we should make this a community project of sorts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> it's an interesting exercise at the very least!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T02:20:27-07:00","id":866728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caelene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas?p=866661#post866661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll third this one, especially with the Ling add-in.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be great with an expansion that included Mycenaean Greece. I've had this idea in my head for the last couple of weeks that Typhon was an Incarnate while Zeus was a Changeling that was a member of the Lost Pantheon. Their fight was so epic that it is still remembered to this day in an embellished form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T02:32:41-07:00","id":866730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas?p=866708#post866708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's another idea: the Mongol Empire era. I mean for many of its subjects, the Mongols must have been this alien, all powerful enemy which came and took what it wanted, reshaping society as it went... sounds pretty Beast-y to me!</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Mongol Empire&quot; is so big that I feel like that needs to get narrowed down a bit for an era entry. I mean, you could have Kubla Khan founding the Yuan Dynasty, fall of the Golden Age of Islam, early Tartar Rus, etc.<br /> <br /> Part of why I like Ivan the Terrible's Russia is you get the multi-ethnic aftermath of the Khanate woven in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T00:46:01-07:00","id":867421,"title":"","content":"Well, I had two ideas for dark eras- <br /> <br /> The Great White North during the Indian/fur trapper days, good possibility for Beasts to interact with native and non native monsters, and either the wendigo are beasts, or another thing for the beasts to interact with.<br /> <br /> And McCarthy Witch Hunts, beasts I imagine have an inherent bit of paranoia, practically anyone they meet could be a hero out to unleash the pitchforks and torches, so an era in which paranoia is rampant could really dial that up to 11.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T20:44:11-07:00","id":868133,"title":"","content":"Child Beasts in the Blitz.<br /> <br /> Kidding.<br /> <br /> Kind of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T20:49:31-07:00","id":868138,"title":"","content":"Just plain Innocents for the Blitz, thanks.<br /> <br /> I still stand by Book of Invasions Ireland.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T20:50:20-07:00","id":868139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas?p=866294#post866294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Hittite Empire during the Bronze Age Collapse would be a good choice because it was a time when the civilizations along the Mediterranean all failed at once. The Bronze Age collapse was probably one of the last times Beasts were actually relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this idea so much. I'm getting ideas for it right now- not even counting the potential for literal Greek Mythological monsters to be up and running as Beasts Rampant or Incarnate. Also, Troy! Trojan War! Intense politics between Mykene and the Hittites!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T08:56:12-07:00","id":868468,"title":"","content":"I still say the Zanzibar Sultanate would make for an excellent Beast Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T09:18:55-07:00","id":868479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas?p=868468#post868468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still say the Zanzibar Sultanate would make for an excellent Beast Era.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting - what about the setting is particularly compelling for Beasts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T17:01:55-07:00","id":868899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas?p=868479#post868479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Interesting - what about the setting is particularly compelling for Beasts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the interest of full disclosure, I should say that my girlfriend is Tanzanian, so I'm a little bit biased in that perspective. Also, I feel very strongly that we need more African Dark Eras, and Beast is as good a place to start with some his any.<br /> <br /> That said, my support for Beast in Zanzibar from the mid-1800s to the mid-1900s is not a coincidence. The capital of the Zanzibar Sultanate, Stone Town, was and still is considered to be a hotbed of the supernatural. Even today, some people make their living in stone town negotiating with Jinn and other spirits. Sometimes this is an act of exorcism, at times it a contract, and sometimes it is negotiation with wayward family. That sounds a lot like Beasts to me.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, The Zanzibar Sultanate represents a time when the African islands are starting to gain more autonomy from the Omani Sultanate, but the crisis of succession still lingers in the air. On the mainland, the British and the Germans are trying to carve out their colonies, driven by fear of losing their resources or be pushed out by other colonial powers. The Sultanate is also framed by a time period when Europe looked at African jungles as being one of the great unknowns. Now that belies their egocentric nature, but I don't think Beasts would care. That's a source of fear that they can feed on, regardless of how poorly justified and racially charged it is. The people of Zanzibar how much better things to fear, such as what happens if the Europeans decide to cross the channel or if the Omani Sultan decides that Zanzibar is still his. There's lots of room for international intrigue there, and plenty of fear to feed the beasts.<br /> <br /> Indigenous African traditions mix with Islam and Arabic traditions, as well as those of the Europeans. It is like a worldwide cultural crossover, which means there are plenty of different supernatural creatures with which Beasts can interact. I also feel compelled to note that the very end of the Zanzibar Sultanate marks the first sighting of a modern African cryptid; the infamous Popobawa, or Bat-wing. Popobawa sightings have continued into the modern-day, and there were riots in Zanzibar from 1970 to 1995 when the creature was sighted. It wouldn't take too much to trace Popobawa's Origins back into an earlier era when the Sultan still ruled.<br /> <br /> All of this points for me to Zanzibar been a lesser known but incredibly interesting setting, with a wide variety of character choices and plot lines to tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 04-19-2016, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T08:43:51-07:00","id":871282,"title":"","content":"I think the best periods for Beast Dark Eras would period of change, cultural clashes and confrontations with the unknown:<br /> <br /> -The Greek Heroic Age<br /> -The period of the Ramayana Epic<br /> -The Punic Wars<br /> -The Germanic and Hunnic Invasions of the Roman Empire<br /> -The Carolingian Empire<br /> -The Mongol Invasions<br /> -The Silk Road at the time of the Black Death<br /> -The Fall of the Inca Empire<br /> -17th Century Angola and the Atlantic Slave Trade<br /> -The Golden Age of Piracy<br /> -The French Revolution and the Reign of Terror<br /> -19th Century Ha\u00efti<br /> -The Indian Wars<br /> -The British Raj<br /> -Post-abolition American-South<br /> -The Russian Revolution<br /> -Occupied Europe during WWII","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T09:24:48-07:00","id":871350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas?p=871282#post871282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the best periods for Beast Dark Eras would period of change, cultural clashes and confrontations with the unknown:<br /> <br /> -Post-abolition American-South</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming you mean the US, and not all of the Americas, this is the one we did.<br /> <br /> And I'd be much much much much more interested in something WWI than WWII. But I know historians tend to be alone in saying we find WWI more interesting than WWII.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T09:37:48-07:00","id":871371,"title":"","content":"Yes, I meant the US.<br /> <br /> In this particular case, I think the responses to the occupation with its collaborators, delators, traitors, resistants and heroes have a horribly fascinating aspect of oppressive dread and paranoia which would make the period perfect for Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T09:46:48-07:00","id":871382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas?p=871371#post871371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I meant the US.<br /> <br /> In this particular case, I think the responses to the occupation with its collaborators, delators, traitors, resistants and heroes have a horribly fascinating aspect of oppressive dread and paranoia which would make the period perfect for Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would definitely be cool. I'm just so WWII'd out. Like, I'm over here wanting to write something about the Belgian Occupation during WWI, where the Germans weaponized rape to try and conceive German children with the Wallonians as psychological torture, etc. Of course, that was also there for WWII. I'm just. So much WWII stuff everywhere. Not much on WWI, despite the recent hundred year anniversary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T10:07:22-07:00","id":871403,"title":"","content":"WWII is omnipresent, isn't it? It's been presented so much as this great fight against absolute evil that it completely captured people's imagination. Comparatively, relatively few people even know what WWI was even about or what happened during that war. Well, at least we'll get a Wonder Woman movie about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T11:14:12-07:00","id":871499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas?p=871403#post871403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WWII is omnipresent, isn't it? It's been presented so much as this great fight against absolute evil that it completely captured people's imagination. Comparatively, relatively few people even know what WWI was even about or what happened during that war. Well, at least we'll get a Wonder Woman movie about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every time someone blames Serbia for WWI, a puppy dies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T12:33:14-07:00","id":871606,"title":"","content":"I think the only government involved in WWI that can be realistically cast as completely blameless is Belgium's. Of course innocent victims are countless in every involved nation separate from their governments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T13:53:05-07:00","id":871702,"title":"","content":"Anteros, you've convinced me that the French Revolution would work really well as a Mage/Beast crossover setting. Apologies to Mummy (which was originally pitched as being in the crossover with Mage in that era during the DE kickstarter), but of course they are getting the Mutapa Empire Mage crossover, so it's all good!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T15:07:55-07:00","id":871767,"title":"","content":"I did?<br /> &gt;.&gt;<br /> &lt;.&lt;<br /> Of course I did!<br /> Beasts would have to be a major part of an era called the Reign of Terror after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":1405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","user":"Anteros","date":". 04-22-2016, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T17:10:22-07:00","id":871893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas?p=871767#post871767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did?<br /> &gt;.&gt;<br /> &lt;.&lt;<br /> Of course I did!<br /> Beasts would have to be a major part of an era called the Reign of Terror after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I figure a usurpation of the Paris Apex would be a central plot point. If it's a Beast overthrowing a Beast, it's definitely a change from Tyrant to Nemesis. On the other hand, either the outgoing or incoming Apex could be a Mage and still influence the entire Hive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T22:17:04-07:00","id":872114,"title":"","content":"It could also be Beasts overthrowing Seers of the Throne, or a conflicts between 2 Beasts/Mages alliances like Tyrants/Seers vs Nemesis/Pentacle (perhaps just adamantine arrows).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T22:49:53-07:00","id":872141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas?p=872114#post872114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could also be Beasts overthrowing Seers of the Throne, or a conflicts between 2 Beasts/Mages alliances like Tyrants/Seers vs Nemesis/Pentacle (perhaps just adamantine arrows).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure the Mage divisions would be that neat. I'm weighing how best to handle it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T23:36:12-07:00","id":872160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas?p=872114#post872114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could also be Beasts overthrowing Seers of the Throne, or a conflicts between 2 Beasts/Mages alliances like Tyrants/Seers vs Nemesis/Pentacle (perhaps just adamantine arrows).</div> </div> </div> </div>There is <b>no</b> Pentacle at time of Reign of Terror - Free Council is still 100 years in making. More to read on our <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/842488-fan-dark-era-french-revolution-mage\">Dark Era in Mage topic</a>.<br /> <br /> I would support this as Beast Era also - Would only point out that beasts, instead to be hard coded alliance, are more like &quot;assets&quot; to use... ee, cooperate with, from Awakened perspective. ANY Family is looking very testy to mages, and any Hunger can have it's purpose.<br /> <br /> They are too fluid to stick them one and another way here, especially as Families and Hungers are very loose coalitions of monsters, not ideology, in the end.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T23:54:15-07:00","id":872173,"title":"","content":"I need to start a separate Mage thread specifically to talk about the French Revolution setting, because I think I've got a grasp on the complicated alliances for the era, but it would be way off topic here.<br /> <br /> For the Paris Apex, I'm thinking before the Revolution its a Seer, but he dies early taken out by revolutionary Mages. A powerful Tyrant rises as Apex ruthlessly imposing order in the Hive to protect Beasts in the chaos of the Revolution. Eventually though, as the Terror begins, she's killed as a counter-revolutionary, and a radical Nemesis rises as Apex.<br /> <br /> I can't decide if its better if the Tyrant is killed by Jacobin Heroes, or the Nemesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-23-2016, 03:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T23:58:15-07:00","id":872175,"title":"","content":"Likes rotation of Apex you propose. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas?p=872173#post872173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need to start a separate Mage thread specifically to talk about the French Revolution setting, because I think I've got a grasp on the complicated alliances for the era, but it would be way off topic here.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have topic for that - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/842488-fan-dark-era-french-revolution-mage\">here it is</a>. I'm really looking to see what you could cook with that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T02:10:57-07:00","id":872224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas#post865860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fiddling with an era hopping game inspired by &quot;Dark Eras&quot;. Besides the Reconstruction Era we're getting in the Dark Eras Companion, what are your choices for compelling fits for BtP. My best developed ideas so far:<br /> <br /> . . .<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2) Vampire crossover for the Jazz Age; Lovecraftian racism at the height of post-civil war racial violence in the US set against the intrigue and beauty of the Harlem Renaissance.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>On a related note, I think a Mine Wars era would be excellent. Turn-of-the-Century society in West Virgina (et al) was fascinating - sort of a mix of cyberpunk (without the computers) and the Wild West. Many of the towns were owned lock, stock, and barrel by the local coal company. They were both your employer and your landlord, your grocery store and the local law enforcement . . . Such a mining town was basically a &quot;coalpunk&quot; arcology. <br /> <br /> And away from the towns? It was pure frontier, where the law was whatever the guy with the most guns said it was. Sometimes even <i>in</i> the towns. Take Hillsville, Va, for example. In 1912, several members of the Allen family were on trial in the local courthouse. The rest of the family didn't like that, so they staged a raid, killing the sheriff, judge . . . much of the local government . . Due to the sudden lack of, well, any surviving local cops, Virginia had to hire a team from Baldwin-Felts to track the Allens down. That's right - its not just a <i>Shadowrun</i> trope (<i>a la</i> Lone Star) - there were actual private law enforcement companies in this era. <br /> <br /> Then there are the Mine Wars themselves. When union organizers really were gun-toting Communist sympathizers looking to overthrow governments, strikebreakers armed themselves with Winchesters and Tommy guns, &quot;accidents&quot; with dynamite were commonplace . . .<br /> <br /> So much violence and greed, such abuses of power and acts of destruction . . . It would've been a heyday for Beasts, who could gorge themselves sick, their feasts completely lost in the background noise. Legends were made, and destroyed, and many of the name from that era are still known today (Mother Jones, anyone?)<br /> <br /> You could also segue directly from it into Prohibition, if you wanted. Many similar themes, in many of the same locations . . .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T03:23:29-07:00","id":872260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas#post865860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2) Vampire crossover for the Jazz Age; Lovecraftian racism at the height of post-civil war racial violence in the US set against the intrigue and beauty of the Harlem Renaissance.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Would buy it, if I could... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T09:43:46-07:00","id":872453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas?p=872224#post872224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a related note, I think a Mine Wars era would be excellent. Turn-of-the-Century society in West Virgina (et al) was fascinating - sort of a mix of cyberpunk (without the computers) and the Wild West. Many of the towns were owned lock, stock, and barrel by the local coal company. They were both your employer and your landlord, your grocery store and the local law enforcement . . . Such a mining town was basically a &quot;coalpunk&quot; arcology.<br /> <br /> And away from the towns? It was pure frontier, where the law was whatever the guy with the most guns said it was. Sometimes even <i>in</i> the towns. Take Hillsville, Va, for example. In 1912, several members of the Allen family were on trial in the local courthouse. The rest of the family didn't like that, so they staged a raid, killing the sheriff, judge . . . much of the local government . . Due to the sudden lack of, well, any surviving local cops, Virginia had to hire a team from Baldwin-Felts to track the Allens down. That's right - its not just a <i>Shadowrun</i> trope (<i>a la</i> Lone Star) - there were actual private law enforcement companies in this era.<br /> <br /> Then there are the Mine Wars themselves. When union organizers really were gun-toting Communist sympathizers looking to overthrow governments, strikebreakers armed themselves with Winchesters and Tommy guns, &quot;accidents&quot; with dynamite were commonplace . . .<br /> <br /> So much violence and greed, such abuses of power and acts of destruction . . . It would've been a heyday for Beasts, who could gorge themselves sick, their feasts completely lost in the background noise. Legends were made, and destroyed, and many of the name from that era are still known today (Mother Jones, anyone?)<br /> <br /> You could also segue directly from it into Prohibition, if you wanted. Many similar themes, in many of the same locations . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>I've wanted to run a Forsaken game in early 20th century or Depression era West Virginia for a long time. Still have the outline for it lying around somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T23:40:20-07:00","id":872923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas?p=872173#post872173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't decide if its better if the Tyrant is killed by Jacobin Heroes, or the Nemesis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm definitely open to opinions on this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T09:07:57-07:00","id":873805,"title":"","content":"Are there any special rules/powers/families/hungers/etc, or just special circumstances/Beast-factions, that would be appropriate for certain Eras to include in Dark Era chapters? Seeing as that's some of the most popular material in the current Dark Eras book...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T03:09:40-07:00","id":874377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/865860-beast-dark-eras-ideas?p=873805#post873805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any special rules/powers/families/hungers/etc, or just special circumstances/Beast-factions, that would be appropriate for certain Eras to include in Dark Era chapters? Seeing as that's some of the most popular material in the current Dark Eras book...</div> </div> </div> </div>For something like the Bronze Age Collapse I would like to see Beasts as describe by the Mummy in the core book. Beasts would probably be about the same except they would mechanically have an easier time feeding (but than again, they might just not be so hungry because eating and spreading your legend was probably easier back then). I'd like to think Beasts stalked through and terrorized communities to keep them aware of the dangers around them.<br /> <br /> What I would really want to see is uncorrupted Heroes. I suspect there powers would probably be more geared towards helping build traumatized people and communities so they arise stronger than they were before and possibly be able to detect supernatural problems that have been tagged by Beasts through Kinship, giving Heroes and Beasts a symbiotic relationship. These powers would probably do things like make it harder for people to fail Integrity checks and help them raise their Integrity. Heroes would still go out and slay Beasts of course, but because of how they track them and their greater awareness of the world around them they would be more likely to find and kill Beasts that terrorized the community because of the problems they cause. Basically Beasts would protect their communities because they feed off humans while Heroes would build up the traumatized and make it easier for those mortals to make it through hardship with a healthy state of mind.<br /> <br /> WWI Beast would be great, but I think it would work better as a Geist crossover. Sin-Eaters were apparently more common than usual on the battlefields. The Beast portion would explore the horrors of war on the streets and in the trenches while Geist would focus on what being a soldier was like.<br /> <br /> Beast/Mage French Revolution sounds really cool.<br /> <br /> A Spanish Inquisition crossover with Hunter could be fun and so could be a solo Era set during the Albigensian Crusade.<br /> <br /> Golden Age of Piracy honestly deserves to be a crossover with everything. All splats have interesting story hooks that could be explored.","sig